WEBVTT

00:00:05.068 --> 00:00:06.820
Who are you?

00:00:06.903 --> 00:00:10.406
Mr. Konta invited us over!

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:11.908
Isn't this just like…

00:00:11.991 --> 00:00:13.785
Our very own reality dating show?

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:16.704
I have a members-only service
where I post all about entrepreneurship.

00:00:16.788 --> 00:00:18.623
Would you like to subscribe to my service?

00:00:18.706 --> 00:00:20.291
I really don't want to get a sunburn.

00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:22.669
Could we swap seats?
Actually, should we just head inside?

00:00:22.752 --> 00:00:24.087
A Pinot Noir from Burgundy?

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.006
If you decant it a bit more,
the aroma will open up.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.677
They sound smart when they talk,
but they feel weirdly shallow.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.762
They are completely empty inside.

00:00:32.846 --> 00:00:34.681
Will Mr. Konta be back soon?

00:00:34.764 --> 00:00:37.392
We came here
because we wanted to talk to him!

00:00:37.475 --> 00:00:40.812
Mr. Konta, the millionaire
who got to retire at a young age.

00:00:41.855 --> 00:00:42.939
Say what?

00:00:47.902 --> 00:00:49.487
TWO HOURS EARLIER

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.365
Radish? One hundred yen?

00:00:52.448 --> 00:00:53.408
These…

00:00:53.908 --> 00:00:56.578
These are turnips. Red turnips.

00:01:00.206 --> 00:01:02.959
Tatsumi Town feels much cooler
compared to Tokyo.

00:01:03.585 --> 00:01:07.088
It seems inbound tourism
is driving up foreign demand around here,

00:01:07.172 --> 00:01:09.090
making it the next big business spot!

00:01:09.174 --> 00:01:11.134
A mentor at a seminar told me.

00:01:11.217 --> 00:01:15.388
Seems like more Japanese business owners
are setting up villas here lately, too.

00:01:16.264 --> 00:01:18.558
We need to expand our network
of wealthy contacts here

00:01:18.641 --> 00:01:21.019
to outmaneuver the other young startups.

00:01:22.145 --> 00:01:23.688
Though, at first glance,

00:01:24.314 --> 00:01:26.649
there doesn't seem to be
anyone wealthy around here.

00:01:26.733 --> 00:01:28.109
Idiot.

00:01:28.192 --> 00:01:31.654
Real millionaires, they wear Uniqlo,

00:01:31.738 --> 00:01:33.072
drive a Vitz,

00:01:33.156 --> 00:01:35.909
and spend their weekends
eating at their villas.

00:01:36.576 --> 00:01:38.828
Ordinary people just see them as ordinary.

00:01:38.912 --> 00:01:40.413
But we're different, right?

00:01:40.496 --> 00:01:42.290
As fellow business professionals,

00:01:42.373 --> 00:01:45.335
we have to spot
the hidden aura within them.

00:01:45.418 --> 00:01:46.544
But listen, like, today,

00:01:46.628 --> 00:01:48.922
these tiny little turnips
were ridiculously cheap!

00:01:49.005 --> 00:01:50.298
Radi? Radi…

00:01:50.381 --> 00:01:51.466
Whatever, they're turnips!

00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:54.677
They were practically giving them away!
So, I bought the entire stock!

00:01:55.261 --> 00:01:57.805
Every single one! See ya later.

00:01:58.389 --> 00:02:00.266
-He said "stock."
-What? She hung up already?

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.060
-Man, Midori…
-Go talk to him!

00:02:02.143 --> 00:02:03.144
You go!

00:02:04.312 --> 00:02:05.521
Excuse me.

00:02:06.731 --> 00:02:08.524
Can we talk for a moment?

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.563
I knew the second I saw you
at the roadside station, Mr. Konta!

00:02:47.647 --> 00:02:49.649
I knew you were someone extraordinary!

00:02:49.732 --> 00:02:50.984
Well, you know,

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:54.153
I do appear on TV a fair bit,
so yes, I guess.

00:02:57.323 --> 00:02:58.199
So?

00:02:58.282 --> 00:03:00.326
What made you so interested in me?

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.411
My young friends.

00:03:01.494 --> 00:03:03.162
Did my aura give me away?

00:03:03.246 --> 00:03:05.790
I guess I just couldn't hide it?

00:03:05.873 --> 00:03:07.500
Yes! You have an aura!

00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:10.503
Please teach us the secret
to your success, Mr. Konta.

00:03:10.586 --> 00:03:12.630
How you became a millionaire
at a young age!

00:03:12.714 --> 00:03:13.631
What?

00:03:14.382 --> 00:03:15.591
"Okuribito"?

00:03:16.718 --> 00:03:19.929
Oh, that movie that won the Oscar?
I wasn't in Departures!

00:03:20.013 --> 00:03:21.139
I didn't star in it!

00:03:21.931 --> 00:03:23.266
He's misunderstanding that?

00:03:23.349 --> 00:03:25.685
They weren't talking about the movie.

00:03:25.768 --> 00:03:28.021
Konta is too stupid.

00:03:28.104 --> 00:03:30.982
But seriously, this villa is incredible!

00:03:31.065 --> 00:03:35.361
After coming here, we know this
is exactly the lifestyle we're aiming for!

00:03:35.445 --> 00:03:37.989
Well, look at you guys. So passionate.

00:03:38.698 --> 00:03:40.491
Are you all in the industry too?

00:03:40.575 --> 00:03:42.368
Yes! We're still
just starting out, though.

00:03:42.452 --> 00:03:44.746
You should have said so earlier!

00:03:44.829 --> 00:03:47.040
I'll listen to whatever you want to share.

00:03:48.291 --> 00:03:49.792
Then to start off,

00:03:49.876 --> 00:03:53.921
what would you say
was your core strength in business?

00:03:54.005 --> 00:03:55.882
Well, let's see…

00:03:56.758 --> 00:03:58.926
I would say business is like…

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:00.178
taming tigers.

00:04:00.261 --> 00:04:01.387
What?

00:04:01.471 --> 00:04:03.514
You were on Business Tigers?

00:04:04.015 --> 00:04:08.478
BUSINESS TIGERS

00:04:09.729 --> 00:04:11.606
I'm betting the full amount.

00:04:12.857 --> 00:04:14.442
He didn't mean that show!

00:04:14.525 --> 00:04:15.485
Wait, what did he mean?

00:04:15.568 --> 00:04:19.655
Konta was talking about
wrangling extras on set.

00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:25.870
But lately, you know,
I'm not really in that phase anymore.

00:04:26.746 --> 00:04:28.373
Incredible.

00:04:58.236 --> 00:05:01.030
Miraculously,
their conversations match up.

00:05:01.114 --> 00:05:02.824
We need to clear up
their misunderstanding fast.

00:05:02.907 --> 00:05:05.284
They're all idiots, so they synced up.

00:05:06.244 --> 00:05:07.328
Hey, Rinrin.

00:05:07.412 --> 00:05:10.790
Could you go tell them that my brother
is just an unsuccessful actor?

00:05:10.873 --> 00:05:13.543
I've already lost interest
in those three morons.

00:05:13.626 --> 00:05:15.420
You're already on a dating app!

00:05:19.257 --> 00:05:21.384
Do we have more guests?

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.430
My brother dragged three people here.

00:05:27.181 --> 00:05:28.224
Oh!

00:05:28.808 --> 00:05:29.684
Turnips!

00:05:30.184 --> 00:05:33.020
So Konta was talking about radishes!

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:36.107
Guess I'll make a salad.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:38.025
You should have some too.

00:05:38.109 --> 00:05:39.277
We're doing a barbecue today!

00:05:40.153 --> 00:05:41.487
No, I…

00:05:41.571 --> 00:05:43.781
Oh, come on. Please stay and eat.

00:05:48.953 --> 00:05:50.163
Okay.

00:05:53.082 --> 00:05:54.250
Mr. Konta.

00:05:54.333 --> 00:05:56.752
The three of us
actually post videos online.

00:05:56.836 --> 00:05:59.505
Would you consider appearing in one?

00:05:59.589 --> 00:06:02.508
I'm sure tons of young people
want to hear your story!

00:06:04.218 --> 00:06:07.096
Of course!
But make sure to film me from this angle.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:09.557
This side of my face looks sharper.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.474
Here, look.

00:06:10.558 --> 00:06:11.767
I see it.

00:06:12.435 --> 00:06:14.854
They post videos? What kind of videos?

00:06:14.937 --> 00:06:17.773
They sent me the link
when we were talking earlier.

00:06:17.857 --> 00:06:20.193
They have 62 subscribers.

00:06:20.276 --> 00:06:21.402
That's so few.

00:06:21.485 --> 00:06:22.945
"The Three Growth Musketeers.

00:06:23.029 --> 00:06:26.782
To aim for FIRE, you must take risks now!"

00:06:26.866 --> 00:06:29.160
It's one of those seminar-style channels!

00:06:30.203 --> 00:06:32.830
And so today, we asked Gen Z success story

00:06:32.914 --> 00:06:36.626
Mr. Konta all about his work-life balance,
here at his villa!

00:06:36.709 --> 00:06:38.669
See you in the next video!

00:06:38.753 --> 00:06:41.380
Buh-bye!

00:06:44.675 --> 00:06:45.676
Thank you so much!

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.512
-Thank you very much!
-How were my looks?

00:06:48.596 --> 00:06:49.639
You were top-tier!

00:06:49.722 --> 00:06:51.807
My look is on point today!

00:06:51.891 --> 00:06:53.851
I'm totally serving!

00:06:53.935 --> 00:06:56.312
Mr. Nishigami, you chopped the firewood?

00:06:56.395 --> 00:06:57.438
Thank you!

00:06:57.521 --> 00:07:00.149
-You were on form!
-I'm going to burn lots.

00:07:00.233 --> 00:07:01.901
-Thank you.
-Konta!

00:07:01.984 --> 00:07:03.444
-Yes.
-We're about to start!

00:07:03.527 --> 00:07:04.528
Okay.

00:07:04.612 --> 00:07:06.822
Oh, right. You should join us.

00:07:06.906 --> 00:07:07.949
Wait, may we?

00:07:08.032 --> 00:07:09.033
Thank you so much!

00:07:09.116 --> 00:07:10.493
Truly a winner at life!

00:07:11.327 --> 00:07:12.870
Come on, you three.

00:07:12.954 --> 00:07:16.207
Come on! Look at you, Tetsuro.
You're working super hard.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.583
Seats.

00:07:24.215 --> 00:07:26.884
Well then, here's to new encounters.

00:07:26.968 --> 00:07:27.927
Cheers!

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.638
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

00:07:32.348 --> 00:07:33.891
Thank you.

00:07:33.975 --> 00:07:35.560
Welcome.

00:07:43.401 --> 00:07:45.611
Is this pork?

00:07:45.695 --> 00:07:47.071
It's not beef.

00:07:47.989 --> 00:07:49.907
My drink is all gone.

00:07:50.533 --> 00:07:53.327
Huh? Is there any sauce? Sauce.

00:07:54.453 --> 00:07:56.998
Hey, pitch in and help! What's with them?

00:07:57.081 --> 00:07:58.749
They're just sitting around!

00:07:59.292 --> 00:08:01.836
They really don't think at all.

00:08:01.919 --> 00:08:03.421
They are empty boys.

00:08:03.504 --> 00:08:07.300
Why did I even want
these three to like me?

00:08:13.848 --> 00:08:17.518
Here! Start grilling your own food!
Thank you.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:20.646
Let's grill it.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:22.064
Should we?

00:08:23.482 --> 00:08:24.525
Watch out.

00:08:26.527 --> 00:08:29.614
Are you members of any online communities?

00:08:30.448 --> 00:08:32.450
Huh? Online communities?

00:08:32.533 --> 00:08:34.869
No, we aren't in any.

00:08:34.952 --> 00:08:37.788
Then how do you build your networks?

00:08:38.831 --> 00:08:40.583
Never mind that, look at your chest.

00:08:40.666 --> 00:08:41.500
There's a bug.

00:08:43.628 --> 00:08:45.838
Oh, no! No, get it off!

00:08:45.921 --> 00:08:47.840
-Calm down.
-What is this?

00:08:47.923 --> 00:08:49.842
-It's just a drone beetle.
-Gross!

00:08:50.468 --> 00:08:51.552
Gross!

00:08:52.219 --> 00:08:54.722
-You're cute.
-A cockroach, so gross.

00:08:54.805 --> 00:08:56.515
Go on back to the forest.

00:08:58.225 --> 00:08:59.268
No! The meat!

00:09:00.311 --> 00:09:03.898
-Oh, crap…
-It's fine. I'll do it. Give.

00:09:12.073 --> 00:09:13.074
It's hot.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:15.826
So hot!

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:18.746
So hot.

00:09:18.829 --> 00:09:19.664
You all right?

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.000
Can't handle bugs.

00:09:23.084 --> 00:09:24.543
Can't grill meat.

00:09:24.627 --> 00:09:26.212
What is up with these guys?

00:09:26.295 --> 00:09:27.755
Right?

00:09:27.838 --> 00:09:30.049
They only came here to network.

00:09:39.725 --> 00:09:43.062
Mr. Konta.
I am so, so glad I got to meet you today!

00:09:43.145 --> 00:09:46.023
Same. I always want to support
young people working hard.

00:09:46.107 --> 00:09:47.858
So, you can ask me for advice anytime.

00:09:47.942 --> 00:09:51.570
I actually want to ask you
something right away.

00:09:51.654 --> 00:09:53.572
Oh, that really is right away.

00:09:53.656 --> 00:09:55.241
-What is it?
-Mr. Konta.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.619
Would you be willing to invest in us?

00:10:06.293 --> 00:10:07.795
-Invest?
-Yes!

00:10:07.878 --> 00:10:09.422
-Me?
-Yes!

00:10:09.505 --> 00:10:10.506
How much?

00:10:13.801 --> 00:10:14.802
10,000 yen?

00:10:14.885 --> 00:10:16.011
No.

00:10:16.095 --> 00:10:17.096
1,000.

00:10:17.888 --> 00:10:18.931
Oh, what?

00:10:19.014 --> 00:10:20.850
"Invest"? What an exaggeration!

00:10:20.933 --> 00:10:21.767
Sure.

00:10:22.351 --> 00:10:23.185
Wait.

00:10:23.269 --> 00:10:24.437
Really?

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:25.438
Incredible.

00:10:25.521 --> 00:10:28.107
I used to borrow money
from my seniors all the time.

00:10:29.734 --> 00:10:31.485
Make sure you pay me back.

00:10:32.611 --> 00:10:33.988
What?

00:10:34.071 --> 00:10:35.156
No.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:37.408
Not one of these.

00:10:37.491 --> 00:10:38.701
Not one?

00:10:38.784 --> 00:10:41.662
What we mean
is an investment in our business.

00:10:41.746 --> 00:10:42.913
Ten thousand of these.

00:10:44.623 --> 00:10:45.875
Say what?

00:10:45.958 --> 00:10:47.501
That's ten million yen!

00:10:48.085 --> 00:10:50.379
Are you out of your mind?
What are you saying?

00:10:50.463 --> 00:10:51.422
I'm an actor.

00:10:51.505 --> 00:10:53.966
No way I have that kind of money!
My savings are under 100,000.

00:10:54.049 --> 00:10:55.050
Wait.

00:10:55.134 --> 00:10:56.635
You're an actor?

00:10:56.719 --> 00:10:57.762
Give it back.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.557
Don't look at my 1,000 yen.

00:11:02.141 --> 00:11:03.851
Hey, look at this.

00:11:05.686 --> 00:11:07.021
SOUSAIDOU ACTORS OFFICE

00:11:07.104 --> 00:11:09.190
This guy is an actor.

00:11:09.273 --> 00:11:10.900
So that means…

00:11:14.195 --> 00:11:15.362
But you were talking stocks.

00:11:15.446 --> 00:11:16.447
Stocks?

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:19.617
Oh! I got a nice stock of turnips!
Did you not have the salad?

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:20.743
What?

00:11:20.826 --> 00:11:23.037
So by stock, you meant these?

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.123
Apparently, they're called radishes.
Or Raditz.

00:11:26.207 --> 00:11:28.250
Like Goku's older brother.

00:11:28.876 --> 00:11:30.085
I see.

00:11:30.169 --> 00:11:32.713
It seems there was a misunderstanding.

00:11:32.796 --> 00:11:35.591
So Mr. Konta, you aren't rich?

00:11:36.217 --> 00:11:37.259
Of course not!

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.015
This is the worst.

00:11:43.098 --> 00:11:45.392
I'm covered in bug bites everywhere.

00:11:45.476 --> 00:11:46.435
It's the worst.

00:11:47.144 --> 00:11:48.187
Jeez, so many bugs!

00:12:05.412 --> 00:12:06.664
The meat!

00:12:16.131 --> 00:12:17.550
Are you okay?

00:12:25.849 --> 00:12:27.017
Excuse me.

00:12:28.269 --> 00:12:29.478
What?

00:12:32.982 --> 00:12:34.441
-Oh, man!
-That was close!

00:12:34.525 --> 00:12:35.943
Can we salvage this?

00:12:36.026 --> 00:12:37.778
You should have hedged the risk.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:41.198
Just go home already! You total airheads!

00:12:41.282 --> 00:12:44.451
From now on, you guys better
call yourselves "The Empty Boys"!

00:12:45.077 --> 00:12:46.870
"The Empty Boys"?

00:12:46.954 --> 00:12:47.955
It's fine.

00:12:48.038 --> 00:12:51.667
An empty head just means
you can stuff more dreams into it!

00:12:55.713 --> 00:12:56.964
Well then…

00:12:57.047 --> 00:12:58.465
Thanks for the food.

00:12:58.549 --> 00:13:00.050
Clean up after yourselves!

00:13:00.134 --> 00:13:01.302
Don't come back!

00:13:01.385 --> 00:13:04.346
Oh, there are tons of bugs
on the way out. So here.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.056
-Thank you.
-You can have it.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.099
Are you sure?

00:13:07.182 --> 00:13:08.642
Thank you.

00:13:08.726 --> 00:13:10.936
-Bye. See you again.
-We'll come again.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:12.187
Thank you!

00:13:18.193 --> 00:13:22.740
Still, I don't think I have any right
to look down on those guys.

00:13:22.823 --> 00:13:23.741
What?

00:13:24.366 --> 00:13:26.452
I think I might be empty too.

00:13:27.036 --> 00:13:29.788
When it comes to work and romance.

00:13:30.956 --> 00:13:32.249
And intelligence?

00:13:33.167 --> 00:13:38.505
But today, I think I finally figured out
who I should really be looking at.

00:13:39.423 --> 00:13:40.716
What's with you?

00:13:49.016 --> 00:13:49.975
Konta.

00:13:50.059 --> 00:13:51.018
Let me help you!

00:13:51.101 --> 00:13:52.519
Oh, Rinrin, thanks.

00:13:53.187 --> 00:13:54.480
Watch out for the ash.

00:13:54.563 --> 00:13:55.773
-Got it.
-All right.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:39.108
Mr. Nishigami!

00:14:41.068 --> 00:14:43.946
Thank you for earlier.

00:14:45.864 --> 00:14:46.949
It was nothing.

00:14:48.409 --> 00:14:49.493
Well…

00:14:50.995 --> 00:14:53.914
I am really grateful.

00:14:55.708 --> 00:14:56.959
Mr. Nishigami…

00:14:58.043 --> 00:15:01.463
You protected me from the fire.

00:15:02.673 --> 00:15:03.590
Well…

00:15:05.968 --> 00:15:06.844
I…

00:15:06.927 --> 00:15:08.470
Please excuse me.

00:15:13.684 --> 00:15:14.768
Mr. Nishigami!

00:15:18.731 --> 00:15:19.982
See you tomorrow!

00:15:43.172 --> 00:15:44.089
Look at this.

00:15:44.173 --> 00:15:45.799
Oh, the video from the other day?

00:15:45.883 --> 00:15:47.051
They actually uploaded it.

00:15:47.134 --> 00:15:48.010
COMMENTS

00:15:48.093 --> 00:15:50.095
-What?
-What's with these comments?

00:15:50.179 --> 00:15:52.723
Huh? Why is everyone talking about stocks?

00:15:52.806 --> 00:15:54.391
Because they're all idiots.

00:15:55.017 --> 00:15:56.477
Hey, look at the channel name.

00:15:57.061 --> 00:15:59.605
"The Empty Boys: We're Gonna Smash It!"

00:15:59.688 --> 00:16:01.315
Huh? I don't get it.

00:16:01.398 --> 00:16:04.985
Well, they weren't dating material,
but maybe they're decent guys?

00:16:05.069 --> 00:16:06.361
Nope. Not at all!

00:16:06.904 --> 00:16:08.572
So harsh. Brutal.

00:16:16.914 --> 00:16:19.166
WE SPOKE TO SUCCESSFUL BUSINESSMAN
KONTA HOSHINO!

00:16:19.249 --> 00:16:21.460
-Isn't this hilarious?
-Yeah.

00:16:21.543 --> 00:16:25.130
I stumbled on it while looking
at a channel run by my college friends!

00:16:25.214 --> 00:16:26.757
This guy isn't bad…

00:16:27.508 --> 00:16:30.719
You know, he might actually
be pretty interesting.

00:16:54.868 --> 00:16:55.828
On me?

00:16:55.911 --> 00:16:57.204
Did something happen to Konta?

00:16:57.287 --> 00:16:59.456
I bet he failed another audition.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.625
Do you know a show called
Document Memoreal?

00:17:01.708 --> 00:17:03.669
They want to do a feature on me.

00:17:03.752 --> 00:17:05.045
Say what?

00:17:05.129 --> 00:17:07.005
-Let me carry that.
-Mr. Nishigami.

00:17:07.089 --> 00:17:09.383
I'm happy for Mr. Konta.

00:17:10.008 --> 00:17:12.803
Good morning.
I'm Torihara from Document Memoreal.

00:17:12.886 --> 00:17:14.012
Why those outfits and makeup?

00:17:14.096 --> 00:17:15.472
We might be on camera too.

00:17:15.556 --> 00:17:17.141
I look forward to working with you all!

00:17:17.766 --> 00:17:20.686
-He's getting carried away.
-Is he really going to be okay?

00:17:20.769 --> 00:17:23.188
He thinks he'll go viral
and become popular.

00:17:23.272 --> 00:17:24.690
You're being tricked.

00:17:24.773 --> 00:17:29.027
I'm the actor, Konta Hoshino.

00:17:29.111 --> 00:17:30.070
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.